  "description": "Temperatures, pressures, flow and high voltage. The live dashboard is owned by Grafana and edited in the UI; grafana/dashboards-archive/ is the copy git tracks (tools/save_dashboard.py --save / --load, see DESIGN.md section 12). Time series are bucketed with $__timeGroupAlias: channels read by different services land on different timestamps, and without bucketing Grafana's long-to-wide pivot produces a frame that is ~50% NULL, so nothing renders at all. Every time-series panel sets a min interval of 10s and maxDataPoints 3000, which is what holds the plots at one point per 10 s - the rate values are actually stored at - out to 8.3 hours, after which the bucket widens on its own. No threshold lines: thresholds live in alarms.yaml and drawing them here would duplicate the number (section 11).",
